etles 20-10=<<20-10=10>>10 maggots in the second feeding\n#### 10"}, {"question": "The largest room in Mrs. McAvoy's house is 45 feet wide and 30 feet long. The smallest room in that same house is 15 feet wide and 8 feet long. What is the difference in area between the largest room and the smallest room?", "answer": "The area of the largest room is 45 ft x 30 ft = <<45*30=1350>>1350 sq ft\nThe area of the smallest room is 15 ft x 8 ft = <<15*8=120>>120 sq ft\nThe difference between the two is 1350 sq ft - 120 sq ft = <<1350-120=1230>>1230 sq ft\n#### 1230"}, {"question": "Michael and Thomas are selling their lego collections. They agree to split any money they earn. They sell them based on how many circles are on top. Each circle costs 1 cent. They earned $5 each after selling 100 single pieces, 45 double pieces, 50 triple pieces and a number of quadruple pieces. How many quadruple pieces did they sell?", "answer": "They made $10 because 2 x 5 = <<2*5=10>>10\nThey made $1 off single pieces because 100 x .01 = <<100*.01=1>>1\nThey made $.9 off double pieces because 45 x .02 = <<45*.02=.9>>.9\nThey made $1.5 off triple pieces because 50 x .03 = <<50*.03=1.5>>1.5\nThey earned $3.4 off the first three types because 1 + .9 + 1.5 = <<1+.9+1.5=3.4>>3.4\nThey earned $6.6 off the quadruple pieces because 10 - 3.4 = <<10-3.4=6.6>>6.6\nThey sold 165 quadruple pieces because 6.6 / .04 = <<6.6/.04=165>>165\n#### 165"}, {"question": "Logan makes $65,000 a year. He spends $20,000 on rent every year, $5000 on groceries every year, and $8000 on gas every year. If he wants to have at least $42000 left, how much more money must he make each year?", "answer": "Logan spends 20000+5000+8000 = <<20000+5000+8000=33000>>33000 a year.\nLogan has 65000-33000 = <<65000-33000=32000>>32000 left a year.\nLogan needs to make 42000-32000 = <<42000-32000=10000>>10000 more a year.\n#### 10,000"}, {"question": "Of 96 oranges, half were ripe. If 1/4 of the ripe oranges were eaten and 1/8 of the unripe 